{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And this is the work of the menorah.</b> This is one of three things that Moses found difficult, and we derive this from the fact that it is written about them 'this' (זה), and that which they did not count [as difficult] — ״זה יתנו כל העובר״ etc. — one may answer that he did not find difficulty in the precise measurement [of the weight], but he himself wondered how HaShem would be satisfied with so light a thing as this; and this is what the liturgical poet composed: במה יתרצה אשכול הכופר." "<b>The work of the menorah.</b> The matter of the craftsmanship of the menorah is stated elsewhere and repeated here on account of the matter of the thigh that is newly taught here, namely that it is stated here: <b>to its thigh, to its flower. So did Moses make</b> the menorah."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:57.709175561Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}